# Netscape HTTP Cookie File
# This file can be used with yt-dlp to provide authentication cookies
# 
# To use this file:
# 1. Rename to 'cookies.txt'
# 2. Export cookies from your browser using a browser extension like:
#    - "cookies.txt" extension for Chrome/Firefox
#    - Or manually extract from browser dev tools
#
# Format: domain	flag	path	secure	expiration	name	value
#
# Example Instagram cookies (replace with real values):
# .instagram.com	TRUE	/	TRUE	1234567890	sessionid	your_session_id_here
# .instagram.com	TRUE	/	FALSE	1234567890	csrftoken	your_csrf_token_here
#
# Example TikTok cookies:
# .tiktok.com	TRUE	/	TRUE	1234567890	sessionid	your_session_id_here
# .tiktok.com	TRUE	/	FALSE	1234567890	csrf_token	your_csrf_token_here
#
# Note: Never commit real cookies to git! Add cookies.txt to .gitignore